{"id": "EUVD-2026-67483", "enisaUuid": "32c9d971-6681-35ed-838f-4df2dd16dcda", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing/probes: Remove WARN_ON_ONCE from parse_btf_arg\n\nSashiko found that user can cause this WARN_ON_ONCE() easily\nwith adding a kprobe event based on a raw address with BTF\nparameter.\n\nSince this is not an unexpected condition, remove the\nWARN_ON_ONCE().", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:48:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24a753a49d06813a156695e3804dcc11c7fdef07", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e177f1530af440d9330c149080aa3b24ddefa18b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f148f86c65b8f9ef2466ad8506e721749e4957fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a662d8c05e2cf16f7a047c81bc1eb5d3b29bacd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/251a8fe1b9aedccd298b77bc28426d564c5a923f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x9r4-5m29-32qp", "CVE-2026-80607"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f48c62c-216a-39b1-bc73-e991c74deddf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b576e09701c7d045bbe5cd85d53e2f34426aa214 <e177f1530af440d9330c149080aa3b24ddefa18b"}, {"id": "13e8d425-6581-39e7-8c10-43b8eab3881f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b576e09701c7d045bbe5cd85d53e2f34426aa214 <24a753a49d06813a156695e3804dcc11c7fdef07"}, {"id": "6576a7b6-6475-3e15-8794-f4eb9fdef44b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b576e09701c7d045bbe5cd85d53e2f34426aa214 <251a8fe1b9aedccd298b77bc28426d564c5a923f"}, {"id": "6b45ef3f-f63a-338c-ba34-23639262ee71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "7ace86fe-596f-368d-8135-b1563e85d877", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b576e09701c7d045bbe5cd85d53e2f34426aa214 <8a662d8c05e2cf16f7a047c81bc1eb